---
alwaysApply: true
---

@rule guardrails
Hard guardrails that MUST be followed. Violations require explicit justification.

## Migrations & Codegen
- If a solution requires DB migration or codegen, RESPOND with:
  "Decline: Migrations and generators are out of scope. Adjust only entities/services per CLAUDE.md."
- NEVER run `yarn migration:generate`, `yarn migration:run`, `nest g`, or similar commands.

## Package Management
- If a command uses npm/pnpm, REWRITE to Yarn.
- Only use: `yarn add`, `yarn remove`, `yarn install`, `yarn upgrade`.

## Controller Boundaries
- If a controller contains business logic (>5 lines of domain logic), MOVE it to service.
- Controllers MUST be thin delegators.

@example controller_violation
// BAD: business logic inline
@Post()
create(@Body() dto: CreateArticleDto) {
  // compute slug, hit cache, emit events...
}

@fix controller_violation
// GOOD: delegate to service
@Post()
create(@Body() dto: CreateArticleDto) {
  return this.svc.create(dto);
}

## Configuration Access
- If accessing process.env directly in feature modules, USE ConfigService instead.

@example env_violation
// BAD: direct process.env access
const dbHost = process.env.DATABASE_HOST;

@fix env_violation
// GOOD: use config service
constructor(private configService: ConfigService) {}
const dbHost = this.configService.get('database.host');

## Analytics Tracking
- If a controller endpoint handles CRUD operations, ENSURE @TrackEvent decorator is present.
- MUST import AnalyticsModule in feature module.

## Permissions
- If an endpoint requires authorization beyond basic auth, USE @RequirePermissions decorator.
- MUST import PermissionsModule in feature module.
